
SCRIPT:Mithril 01
"Thorin once gave a shirt of mithril mail to Bilbo..."
END

SCRIPT:Mithril 02
"That was a kingly gift!"
END

SCRIPT:Mithril 03
"Indeed. I never told him, but its worth is greater than half the Shire..."
END

SCRIPT:Throne 01
"The throne of Durin! This is a hallowed place."
END

SCRIPT:Throne 02
"So did you know him, this Durin?"
END

SCRIPT:Throne 03
"It has been a very long time since Durin walked among us."
END

SCRIPT:Throne 04
"The Dwarves of Durin's House believe Durin will be reincarnated seven times."
END

SCRIPT:Throne 05
"Oh, I see. So what's the current tally?"
END

SCRIPT:Throne 06
"I will forgive your insolence, master Peregrin, because I know that you cannot help it. "
END

SCRIPT:Library 01
"The Dwarves of Khazad-dum were dilligent scribes, recording a great many things in close detail."
END

SCRIPT:Library 02
"We Dwarves take great pride and joy in documenting our lineage through far-branching family trees and tales of the deeds of our fathers."
END

SCRIPT:Library 03
"Your kin is not so different from ours."
END

SCRIPT:Library 04
"We shouldn't linger here."
END

SCRIPT:Library 05
"Indeed! We could not read these tomes even if we had time... the language of the Dwarves is a well-kept secret."
END

SCRIPT:Library 06
"It is to most."
END

SCRIPT:Armoury 01
"I did not look to find these blades in Moria. They are of Noldorin make!"
END

SCRIPT:Armoury 02
"In another age, when Khazad-dum flourished, its inhabitants maintained close friendship with the Elves of Eregion."
END

SCRIPT:Armoury 03
"It was Celebrimbor himself who drew the signs on the Doors of Durin. The Elves had free passage into Khazad-dum for many years."
END

SCRIPT:Drum 01
"Without that drum, many of these vile Goblins will be blind to our passage."
END

SCRIPT:Map 01
"This map records that the western and southern passages through Moria were overrun by Goblins."
END

SCRIPT:Map 02
"We should take the eastern road when we can."
END

SCRIPT:Axe 01
"By my beard! This is the axe of Durin."
END

SCRIPT:Axe 02
"So it is, Gimli. Keep it to hand! We may have need of it ere we reach the Mirrormere..."
END

SCRIPT:Axe Hint
"Gimli has retrieved Durin's Axe. He will now deal increased damage"
END

SCRIPT:Muzgash Dead
"Muzgash! That brute has finally fallen."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim01
"Gandalf: These papers record the fate of Balin's expedition to reclaim this place..."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim02
"Rally together, my kinsmen! We must hold them here, until Oin secures the West-gate!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim03
"Quick! Clear out these wretched Orcs!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim04
"Balin! The West-gate is overrun! Disaster is upon us! An army of Orcs approach from the East!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim05
"Balin: We cannot win here. We must retreat to the Second Hall and recover our strength."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim06
"Let us make haste!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim013
"Lend us a hand, would you? We're surrounded! "
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim07
"Durin's Beard! My dear Ori! You yet live!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim07B
"Lord Balin! Come, we must defend this hall, and secure the passage south!"
END


SCRIPT:Reclaim08
"Oin: The Orcs have gathered a great force, and our scouts report terrible sounds coming from the Deeps."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim09
"We must reach the Second Hall, with all haste!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim10
"That is where the account ends.."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim11
"We must not linger here... I should like to find the Hall of Records."
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim11B
"Do you mean the Chamber of Mazarbul?"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim12
"Lord Balin! The Orcs have taken this passage! We will try to hold them off while you find another way!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim13
"With me! We must clear the upper floors quickly!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim14
"Look out! They have broken through the eastern entrance!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim16
"We must find a way through, away from here!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim17
"Lord Balin, retreat along the east road. We will hold them off!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim18
"Lord Balin! Leave us to it, and retreat to safety!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim19
"Quick, move along! We will cover your retreat!"
END

SCRIPT:Reclaim20
"Lord Balin, help us clear this passage."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli078
"These are not holes. Of old, Khazad-dum was full of light and splendour, as is still remembered in our songs."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli085
"The world was young, the mountains green, No stain yet on the Moon was seen, No words were laid on stream or stone. When Durin woke and walked alone."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli086
"He named the nameless hills and dells; He drank from yet untasted wells; He stooped and looked in Mirrormere, And saw a crown of stars appear, As gems upon a silver thread, Above the shadow of his head."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli087
"The world was fair, the mountains tall, In Elder Days before the fall, Of mighty kings in Nargothrond And Gondolin, who now beyond The Western Seas have passed away: The world was fair in Durin's Day."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli088
"A king he was on carven throne, In many-pillared halls of stone, With golden roof and silver floor, And runes of power upon the door."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli089
"The light of sun and star and moon, In shining lamps of crystal hewn, Undimmed by cloud or shade of night, There shone for ever fair and bright."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli090
"There hammer on the anvil smote, There chisel clove, and graver wrote; There forged was blade, and bound was hilt; The delver mined, the mason built."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli091
"There beryl, pearl, and opal pale, And metal wrought like fishes' mail, Buckler and corslet, axe and sword. And shining spears were laid in hoard."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli092
"Unwearied then were Durin's folk; Beneath the mountains music woke: The harpers harped, the minstrels sang, And at the gates the trumpets rang."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli093
"The world is grey, the mountains old, The forge's fire is ashen-cold; No harp is wrung, no hammer falls: The darkness dwells in Durin's halls."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli094
"The shadow lies upon his tomb In Moria, in Khazad-dum."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli095
"But still the sunken stars appear In dark and windless Mirrormere; There lies his crown in water deep, Till Durin wakes again from sleep."
END

SCRIPT:StoryofDurinHint
"Return to the hall to hear the remainder of the Song of Durin."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam111
"There must have been a mighty crowd of Dwarves here at one time. Surely they didn't live in these darksome holes?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin006
"With me, Dwarves!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin007
"We must clear a path through these orcs!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin008
"Come on lads, we must keep moving!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin009
"The path is clear, come on!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin010
"Durin be with you!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin011
"These vile orcs will pay for desecrating our halls!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin012
"Rally together, Dwarves!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin013
"They come again!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin014
"Archers, aim for those Trolls!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin015
"Stand strong Dwarves!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin016
"Baruk-Khazad!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin017
"Khazad ai-menu!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_balin018
"Igribi d'dum!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_merry037
"It's lucky that the tomb wasn't crushed by this massive rock when it fell."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli119
"It is a tomb."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli120
"By my beard! This place... untouched by Orcish filth... could it be? Is this Durin's Rest?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli121
"That axe... that must be Durin's. By Mahal, I will carry it out of here and keep it safe, so that one day it may be returned to its rightful wielder."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli122
"Luck? No. I'll bet half my beard that it was Balin's folk that sealed off all entryways into Durin's Rest."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf319
"It appears so, my dear Dwarf. A hallowed place, of great import."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf245
"Its edge is said to never dull. Keep it to hand, Gimli. We may have need of it ere we reach the Mirrormere."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli123
"There is much you may yet learn from the loremasters of Khazad-dum."
End
